  "hindi": "वह देव सविता प्रेरणा के लिए उठ खड़ा हुआ है; अत्यन्त निरन्तर, उस कार्य से वाहक खड़ा हुआ है। अब वह देवों के लिए रत्न बाँटता है, फिर उसने जिसकी आहुति स्वीकार्य है उसे कल्याण में भाग दिया।",
  "english": "That god Savitṛ has stood up for the impulse; most constantly, by that work, the bearer has stood. Now he apportions treasure to the gods, and then he has given a share to the one whose offering is welcome, in well-being.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Line a is unclear: 'tad apā' (read tat + apā 'by work', inst. of apas) and the placing of 'śaśvattamam' are tentative; vahniḥ 'the bearer' is not identified (the verb asthāt is shared with ud). vītihotram: 'one whose offering is welcome', possibly a name (Vītihotra) or epithet of the sacrificer; not decided. ābhajat 'assigned a share' tentative. dhāti: injunctive 3 sg. of vi-√dhā read as present.",
  "confidence": "low",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.038.1a",
   "002.038.1b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
