  "hindi": "सब की आज्ञा-पालन के लिए, देव ऊपर उठा हुआ, चौड़े हाथों वाला, दोनों भुजाओं से आगे बढ़ता है। जल भी उसके व्रत में झुके हुए हैं; यह वायु भी परिभ्रमण में विश्राम करता है।",
  "english": "For the obedience of all, the god, upright, broad-handed, stretches forth with both arms. Even the waters, bent down, are in his ordinance; even this wind comes to rest in the circuit.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "nimṛgrāḥ is uncertain ('bent down, brought low'); 'ā' is placed with vrate in the printed text and its force is unclear. viśvasya śruṣṭaye: 'for the obedience of all' tentative; śruṣṭi 'obedience, readiness'. parijman 'in the circuit' (loc.) tentative.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.038.2a",
   "002.038.2b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
   "विश्व॑स्य॒ हि श्रु॒ष्टये॑ दे॒व ऊ॒र्ध्वः प्र बा॒हवा॑ पृ॒थुपा॑णि॒: सिस॑र्ति",
   "आप॑श्चिदस्य व्र॒त आ निमृ॑ग्रा अ॒यं चि॒द् वातो॑ रमते॒ परि॑ज्मन्"
  ],
  "lines_iast": [
